{
  "schema": "hymn-palette/1",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "owner": "art (M1-ART-01)",
  "color_space_note": "hex is sRGB-encoded (what you type into a Godot color picker). linear is the sRGB EOTF of that hex, rounded to 4 places, which is what shaders and the renderer use. luminance_linear is Rec.709 relative luminance.",
  "value_kinds_note": "Every swatch has two kinds of value. INPUT: hex/linear, what you type into a material, light, sky or shader parameter. ON-SCREEN: onscreen_hex, what that input shows after exposure and the AgX tonemap, measured on the swatch card (game/levels/_tests/swatches/, shot swatch_card). input_kind says where the input goes. UI swatches are drawn after the tonemap, so their hex IS the on-screen value and they have no onscreen_hex. See README.md, 'Two kinds of colour value'.",
  "onscreen_reference": {
    "grade": "AgX (Environment.tonemap_mode 4), tonemap_agx_white 12, tonemap_agx_contrast 1.25 (engine default), no adjustment, no glow, no fog, no LUT; Godot 4.6.3 Forward+, measured on lavapipe",
    "levels": "Scene-referred level k = exposure x incident light. -1 = k 0.5, 0 = k 1.0, +1 = k 2.0. Albedo: k = tonemap_exposure x (key energy x N.L + fill). Emission: k = tonemap_exposure x emission energy. Light colour: the swatch is a white (albedo 1) card lit at k. Sky colour: k = tonemap_exposure x sky_energy_multiplier.",
    "tool": "godot-render ... res://game/levels/_tests/swatches/swatch_measure.tscn -- --out=<json> (reproduces Rendering's M1-ART-01 review values to within 2/255)",
